=== DESIGN ===

OBJECTIVE
The units package is the single place in the Tesla telemetry pipeline
where producer-emitted numeric values get converted to canonical SI.
Per ADR-004 #4 the rule is "every unit-bearing field is converted to
canonical SI at one place," and this prompt establishes that one place.

ToSI is intentionally a 3-arg pure function:

    ToSI(field string, raw float64, active ActiveUnit) (float64, error)

The third argument is non-negotiable — the 2-arg form (field, raw) would
imply a hardcoded wire-unit assumption (e.g. "always assume km for
distance"), which is wrong: Tesla emits values in either mi or km
depending on the per-vehicle SettingDistanceUnit at sample time, and
the active unit can transition mid-day. The unit-history layer
(prompt 0022) materialises the active unit per (vehicle, sample-time);
the normalize pipeline (prompt 0028) joins it onto every Atomic and
calls ToSI. ToSI itself owns no I/O and no state — it is a pure
function over (field, raw, active).

PACKAGE LAYOUT
  types.go        ActiveUnit constants + sentinel errors
  conversions.go  conversion tables (per-UnitKind and per-speed-field)
  units.go        ToSI dispatcher
  units_test.go   table-driven coverage of every conversion arm

ACTIVE-UNIT CONSTANTS
The set is closed and matches the four SettingUnit enums emitted by
Tesla Fleet Telemetry:

    SettingDistanceUnit    -> {ActiveUnitMiles, ActiveUnitKilometers}
    SettingTemperatureUnit -> {ActiveUnitFahrenheit, ActiveUnitCelsius}
    SettingTirePressureUnit-> {ActiveUnitPSI, ActiveUnitBar}
    SettingChargeUnit      -> {ActiveUnitDistance, ActiveUnitPercent}

The ChargeUnit pair is informational (it tells the UI which form to
prefer when rendering range-vs-percent), not a numeric conversion: the
SoC scalar itself is always emitted in % and never needs unit
conversion. The conversion table therefore has no entry for
UnitKindCharge — a deliberate gap so an attempt to convert SoC returns
ErrUnsupportedUnit and the caller is forced to think about whether the
operation makes sense.

ERROR SENTINELS
Three errors, sorted by severity:

  ErrNoUnitContext   the caller did not supply an active unit (active=="").
                     This is what the normalize pipeline returns when it
                     looked up unit_history and found no row for the
                     (vehicle, sample-time) — typically because the
                     vehicle joined mid-cohort and we have not yet
                     observed a SettingDistanceUnit emission. ToSI does
                     NOT silently default to one of the units because
                     "default to km" would silently corrupt a US car.
                     Caller drops the value and increments a counter.

  ErrUnsupportedField the field is either unknown or non-unit-bearing.
                     Returned for {"PackVoltage", "DriveRail", ...} and
                     for typos. The prompt's gate phrasing "field not
                     unit-bearing" covers both arms.

  ErrUnsupportedUnit  the active unit is incompatible with the field's
                     UnitKind, e.g. an Odometer (Distance) with an
                     active unit of "psi". Returned by both the regular
                     conversion path (table miss in the inner map) and
                     the speed-override path (speedConversions miss).

CONVERSION TABLES
The regular table is keyed first by protomodel.UnitKind, then by
ActiveUnit. Each entry is a single closure that takes the raw producer
value and returns SI:

  UnitKindDistance:   miles -> meters,        km -> meters
  UnitKindTemperature: F    -> C,             C  -> C
  UnitKindPressure:   psi   -> Pascals,       bar-> Pascals

Math constants:

  miles->meters     1609.344     (exact; international mile = 1760 yards
                                  * 0.9144 m/yard)
  km   ->meters     1000.0       (exact)
  F    ->C          (F-32)*5/9   (exact)
  C    ->C          identity     (already canonical)
  psi  ->Pa         6894.757     (NIST SP 811 conversion factor; one
                                  pound-force per square inch in
                                  pascals)
  bar  ->Pa         100000.0     (exact)

SPEED OVERRIDE
VehicleSpeed (Field=4) and CruiseSetSpeed (Field=101) are linear
velocities that follow SettingDistanceUnit (mph in US, km/h in EU) but
their canonical SI form is m/s — NOT meters. The signal_metadata_gen.go
classifier correctly leaves them as UnitKindNone because UnitKindDistance
would imply meters as the SI form, which is wrong for a velocity.

The speed-override path runs BEFORE the UnitKindNone gate so these two
fields remain convertible. (A more principled fix would be to introduce
a UnitKindSpeed in protomodel/types.go, but that is out of scope for
this prompt — the metadata is generated and adding a new UnitKind would
also require updating the codegen, the coverage test's deny-list, and
the unit-history layer all at once. The speed-override list is the
forward-compatible workaround.)

The DiAxleSpeed{R,F,REL,RER} and HvacFanSpeed fields are explicitly
NOT in the speed-override list — they carry rotational speed (RPM /
fan-level) and do not convert linearly with SettingDistanceUnit.

Speed conversions:

  mph  -> m/s   raw * 0.44704                  (= 1609.344 / 3600)
  km/h -> m/s   raw * (1000.0 / 3600.0)        (= 0.27778...)

ALGORITHM
Per the prompt's pseudo-code, with one ordering deviation noted above
(speed-override before UnitKindNone gate, because VehicleSpeed/
CruiseSetSpeed have UnitKindNone in metadata):

  1. lookup meta := protomodel.SignalsByName[field]
     - miss -> ErrUnsupportedField (wraps with %q)
  2. if isSpeedField(field):
       - active=="" -> ErrNoUnitContext
       - speedConversions[active] miss -> ErrUnsupportedUnit
       - else -> return fn(raw)
  3. if meta.UnitKind == UnitKindNone -> ErrUnsupportedField
  4. if active == "" -> ErrNoUnitContext
  5. conversions[meta.UnitKind][active] miss -> ErrUnsupportedUnit
  6. return fn(raw)

PURITY
ToSI imports nothing from net/http, database/sql, jackc/pgx, or any
Redis client. The gate test asserts this with a literal-substring
forbidden-import check. The package's only non-stdlib import is
internal/tesla/protomodel (for UnitKind and SignalsByName).

THREAD-SAFETY
The conversion tables are package-level vars initialised at program
load and never mutated; they are safe to read concurrently. ToSI takes
no locks. The race-detector test (-race in the gate) verifies this.

=== TABLE_TESTS ===

The units_test.go file is purely table-driven — one TestToSI function
with a []struct{ name, field; raw; active; want; wantErrIs } slice and
a per-row t.Run subtest. The table covers every conversion arm at
least once:

DISTANCE (5 fields x 2 units = 10 rows):
  Odometer            mi=1     -> 1609.344 m
  Odometer            km=1     -> 1000     m
  RatedRange          mi=200   -> 321868.8 m
  RatedRange          km=300   -> 300000   m
  EstBatteryRange     mi=150   -> 241401.6 m
  EstBatteryRange     km=240   -> 240000   m
  IdealBatteryRange   mi=180   -> 289681.92 m
  IdealBatteryRange   km=290   -> 290000   m
  MilesToArrival      mi=10    -> 16093.44 m
  MilesToArrival      km=15    -> 15000    m

TEMPERATURE (5 fields x 2 units = 10 rows):
  DiHeatsinkTR    F=32  -> 0    C
  DiHeatsinkTR    C=25  -> 25   C
  DiStatorTempR   F=212 -> 100  C
  DiStatorTempR   C=-40 -> -40  C
  ModuleTempMax   F=68  -> 20   C
  ModuleTempMax   C=37  -> 37   C
  InsideTemp      F=72  -> 22.222... C
  InsideTemp      C=21  -> 21   C
  OutsideTemp    F=-40 -> -40  C
  OutsideTemp    C=0   -> 0    C

PRESSURE (4 fields x 2 units = 8 rows):
  TpmsPressureFl  psi=32 -> 220632.224 Pa
  TpmsPressureFl  bar=2.2-> 220000     Pa
  TpmsPressureFr  psi=33 -> 227527.0   Pa (approx)
  TpmsPressureFr  bar=2.3-> 230000     Pa
  TpmsPressureRl  psi=30 -> 206842.71  Pa
  TpmsPressureRl  bar=2.0-> 200000     Pa
  TpmsPressureRr  psi=31 -> 213737.467 Pa
  TpmsPressureRr  bar=2.1-> 210000     Pa

SPEED (1 field x 2 units = 2 rows, plus one more for coverage):
  VehicleSpeed   mi=60  -> 26.8224 m/s
  VehicleSpeed   km=100 -> 27.777... m/s
  CruiseSetSpeed mi=70  -> 31.2928 m/s

ERROR PATHS:
  Odometer       active=""        -> ErrNoUnitContext
  PackVoltage    active="mi"       -> ErrUnsupportedField (UnitKindNone)
  Odometer       active="psi"      -> ErrUnsupportedUnit
  NotARealField  active="mi"       -> ErrUnsupportedField (unknown)
  VehicleSpeed   active=""         -> ErrNoUnitContext (speed override path)
  VehicleSpeed   active="psi"      -> ErrUnsupportedUnit (speed override path)
  Soc            active="charge_percent" -> ErrUnsupportedUnit
                  (UnitKindCharge has no entries — SoC is always %)

Float comparisons use math.Abs(got-want) <= eps where eps depends on
the row's scale (1e-9 for unity-magnitude conversions, 1e-3 for
pressures whose constants carry only six significant figures).

